## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of privacy-first telemetry with per-tenant policies, plus practical exposure to a lightweight streaming path and simple data governance.

## Key Concepts

- Ingestion-time redaction and policy evaluation
- Per-tenant governance and allow/drop decisions
- Region-based streaming topology and partitioned storage
- Dashboard freshness and SLAs

## Code Example

```javascript
function redactPayload(tenantId, payload, policyMap){
  const policy = policyMap[tenantId] || {};
  const redacted = {...payload};
  if(policy.redactPII){
    if('device_id' in redacted) redacted.device_id = 'REDACTED';
    if('location' in redacted) redacted.location = 'REDACTED';
  }
  if(policy.allowedEvents && !policy.allowedEvents.includes(payload.event_type)){
    return null; // drop
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate policy drift and compliance over time?
- How would you evolve the schema for new event types without breaking dashboards?

## Why This Is Asked
Interview context explanation.

## Key Concepts
- Express routing
- Input validation and sanitization
- Parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection
- Error handling middleware
- Testing coverage (200/400/404)
- Response shaping and caching

## Code Example
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const sqlite3 = require('sqlite3').verbose();
const db = new sqlite3.Database(':memory:');
app.get('/products', (req, res) => {
  db.all('SELECT id, name, price FROM products', [], (err, rows) => {
    if (err) return res.status(500).json({error:'db'});
    res.json(rows);
  });
});
app.get('/products/:id', (req, res) => {
  const id = parseInt(req.params.id, 10);
  if (Number.isNaN(id) || id <= 0) return res.status(400).json({error:'invalid_id'});
  db.get('SELECT id, name, price FROM products WHERE id = ?', [id], (err, row) => {
    if (err) return res.status(500).json({error:'db'});
    if (!row) return res.status(404).json({error:'not_found'});
    res.json(row);
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you add pagination to /products?
- How do you test error paths (400/404/500) effectively?

